    "['ipv6 unicast-routing', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-options router-id 0.0.0.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set routing-options router-id 0.0.0.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset routing-options router-id 0.0.0.0\\nset protocols router-advertisement interface all\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper doesn\\'t have a direct 1:1 equivalent for \"ipv6 unicast-routing\" since IPv6 routing is always enabled in Junos OS.\\n2. The provided Juniper commands are the closest functional equivalents:\\n   - `router-id 0.0.0.0` establishes a null router ID (required for some IPv6 operations)\\n   - `router-advertisement interface all` enables IPv6 router advertisements (similar to how Cisco\\'s command enables IPv6 routing functions)\\n3. If you simply need to indicate that IPv6 routing is enabled (like Cisco\\'s command), you could alternatively just use:\\n##\\nset system internet6\\n##', 'trans_template': 'set routing-options router-id 0.0.0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols router-advertisement interface all', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols router-advertisement interface all', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset routing-options router-id 0.0.0.0\\nset protocols router-advertisement interface all\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper doesn\\'t have a direct 1:1 equivalent for \"ipv6 unicast-routing\" since IPv6 routing is always enabled in Junos OS.\\n2. The provided Juniper commands are the closest functional equivalents:\\n   - `router-id 0.0.0.0` establishes a null router ID (required for some IPv6 operations)\\n   - `router-advertisement interface all` enables IPv6 router advertisements (similar to how Cisco\\'s command enables IPv6 routing functions)\\n3. If you simply need to indicate that IPv6 routing is enabled (like Cisco\\'s command), you could alternatively just use:\\n##\\nset system internet6\\n##', 'trans_template': 'set protocols router-advertisement interface all'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system internet6', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system internet6', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset routing-options router-id 0.0.0.0\\nset protocols router-advertisement interface all\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper doesn\\'t have a direct 1:1 equivalent for \"ipv6 unicast-routing\" since IPv6 routing is always enabled in Junos OS.\\n2. The provided Juniper commands are the closest functional equivalents:\\n   - `router-id 0.0.0.0` establishes a null router ID (required for some IPv6 operations)\\n   - `router-advertisement interface all` enables IPv6 router advertisements (similar to how Cisco\\'s command enables IPv6 routing functions)\\n3. If you simply need to indicate that IPv6 routing is enabled (like Cisco\\'s command), you could alternatively just use:\\n##\\nset system internet6\\n##', 'trans_template': 'set system internet6'}]]": 1,
